On CHERI targets, set the maximum degree of bounds tightening for
userspace programs and libraries.
The default value is
.Li conservative
on CHERI targets and
.Li none
on other targets.
Values are cumulative:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Li none
Default for the target (no flags passed to the compiler)
.It Li conservative
Stack allocations
.It Li references-only
C++ references that are a fixed size
.It Li subobject-safe
When taking a pointer to a subobject of a struct
.It Li aggressive
On individual array entries in
.Li &array[index]
expressions where
.Va index
is non-constant
.It Li very-aggressive
On individual array entries in
.Li &array[index]
expressions where
.Va index
is a constant
.It everywhere-unsafe
Everywhere there is no opt-out including members of unions
.El
Individual program or library Makefiles opt in by setting
.Va CHERI_SUBOBJECT_BOUNDS_MAX
to a value other than
.Li conservative
before including
.In bsd.lib.mk
or
.In bsd.prog.mk .
.Pp
Values above
.Li subobject-safe
increasingly diverge from
.St -isoC
and must be written in an incresingly stylized manner.
